+- **Trust**: external event text is rendered/wrapped as untrusted data (`events.render_event_text`, `safety.wrap_untrusted`); commands pass a denylist then a reviewer model that fails closed (`safety.py`); `external_send` goes through the approval flow (a pending approval gets one nudge after `AOA_APPROVAL_NUDGE`, default 4h, and expires after `AOA_APPROVAL_EXPIRE`, default 24h, driven by `SessionWorkflow` timers guarded by `workflow.patched("approval-expiry")`; an expired approval cannot be approved late); only user-started turns (`trigger_user`) may create routines, and `send_user` turns an `update` into a `reply` in those turns so quiet hours never hold an answer. PR reviews post as a real APPROVE / REQUEST_CHANGES only through the reviewer identity (`gh_reviewer.py`: `AOA_REVIEWER_APP_ID` + key file, or `AOA_REVIEWER_TOKEN`; off when unset), falling back to a comment review on any failure. Merging a PR is never a model tool: only a Slack [Merge] click on an approved review card (an opaque offer id stored by `publish_pr_review`) starts `MergePrWorkflow`, which pins the reviewed commit. On conflicts it resolves them in a temp clone and pushes (`pr_resolve.py`; token only via `GIT_CONFIG_*` env, tests run with an allowlisted env), and the new commit needs its own review and click. It refuses while GitHub auto-merge is on (checked before cloning and again before the push), never pushes a clean merge (`no_conflict`: GitHub's status was stale), and requires every line outside the conflict hunks to survive verbatim (`finish_resolution`). Failure `action`s in `pr_merge.RETRYABLE` bring the card's Merge button back; `needs_human`, `stale` and `tests_failed` do not. Per-repo test command: `AOA_TEST_COMMANDS` > `.aoa/test-command` as it is on the base branch (never the PR's) > pytest in a fresh venv. Those tests run as your user, not in a container (#21 was skipped on purpose), so the resolver is for your own PRs only.
 - `notify.Notifier` decides whether outbound messages go now or are held in a digest (min interval, quiet hours); replies/questions/approvals/urgent always go. Held updates are delivered by a durable timer: `SessionWorkflow` asks `digest_status` for `Notifier.next_flush_at` after each turn and wakes at that time to run `flush_digest` (idempotent client key; guarded by `workflow.patched("digest-flush")`).
